From e066183583984a7db6b9a8d49ed099ffd2e40eff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sachin Kumar Garg <sachin.garg@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:06:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] arm64: dts: qcom: lemans-draco-evk: add video-firmware
 iommu node

lemans-draco-evk-som.dtsi inlines the Lemans EL2-hosting device-tree
modifications normally applied via the lemans-el2.dtbo overlay, but
missed the video-firmware child node under &iris that the overlay
also provides.

Without this node, IRIS has no fw_dev, so it takes the firmware-load
path meant for boards with an external hypervisor managing the SHM
bridge. Since Draco hosts EL2 in Linux itself, TrustZone rejects the
un-bridged firmware buffer with -EINVAL, and IRIS firmware load fails.

Add the missing video-firmware iommu node (same SID as
lemans-el2.dtso) so firmware loading uses the correct self-managed
TZMem path on Draco.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Sachin Kumar Garg <sachin.garg@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-draco-evk-som.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-draco-evk-som.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-draco-evk-som.dtsi
index 7812d1d24152..7a011d3a1772 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-draco-evk-som.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-draco-evk-som.dtsi
@@ -256,6 +256,10 @@
 	firmware-name = "qcom/vpu/vpu30_p4_s6_16mb.mbn";
 
 	status = "okay";
+
+	video-firmware {
+		iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x0882 0x0400>;
+	};
 };
 
 &pmm8654au_0_pon_resin {
